.Dd July 26, 2026
.Dt FINALIZE_UPDATE 8
.Os FreeBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm finalize_update
.Nd swap a -new clone into place after a successful update
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl s Ar name
.Op Fl k Ar kind
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is part of the parasa framework for FreeBSD system management.
It performs the destructive swap after
.Xr update 8
has built and validated a
.Dq -new
clone.
This is the only command in the update flow that destroys the old clone.
.Pp
The finalization proceeds as follows:
.Bl -enum
.It
Verify that
.Ao Ar name Ac Ns -new
exists on zbereshit.
.It
If the target is a container and is running, stop it with
.Xr jail 8 .
.It
Destroy the old clone:
.Cm zfs destroy -r zbereshit/{kind}s/ Ns Ao Ar name Ac .
.It
Rename -new to plain:
.Cm zfs rename Ao Ar name Ac Ns -new Ao Ar name Ac .
.It
Update the
.Pa .foundation
file with the new artifact name.
.It
Save state by delegating to
.Xr save 8 .
.It
For containers, start the jail.
For systems with
.Fl n ,
set
.Xr nextboot 8 .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-k KIND"
.It Fl h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.It Fl d
Dry run.
Show what would be done without making changes.
.It Fl s Ar name
Specify the workspace name.
This option is required.
.It Fl k Ar kind
Specify "system" or "container".
Auto-detected from recipes directory if omitted.
.It Fl n
Set
.Xr nextboot 8
after finalize (systems only).
.El
.Sh ROLLBACK
Before running
.Nm ,
if the -new clone is bad:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zfs destroy -r zbereshit/{kind}s/<name>-new
.Ed
.Pp
Once
.Nm
completes, the swap is irreversible short of re-running
.Xr update 8
with the old artifact.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr update 8 ,
.Xr save 8 ,
.Xr zfs-destroy 8 ,
.Xr zfs-rename 8 ,
.Xr nextboot 8
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
utility is part of the parasa framework.
